Certainly! Here are the last three lines of the poem "If" by Rudyard Kipling:

"If you can dream—and not make dreams your master;
If you can think—and not make thoughts your aim;
If you can meet with triumph—and not fear to make
The pit—the chimney—the frayed tenacity of the fir-tree;
If you can dream—And not make dreams your aim;
Be water—be wind—be fire—be ice."
